! Work handoff — to the `lares(Codex)` nakama-crew, 2026-09-14

''Addressed, dated, and readable cold.'' The founding hearth (`session_01Jg969FCpJcM84XvtsDNFou`) hands the loops below to the `lares(Codex)` crew the operator invited on 2026-09-14. A hand reading this carrier alone holds enough to act: every item names its evidence at file:line or commit, separates what the operator RULED from what stands OPEN, names the ''precondition'' that blocks it, and carries the traps that cost this tree measured hours.

''What this carrier withholds, and where each lives instead.''

* ''The shift ledger'' — <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/handoff">>. It hands one watch to the next among sessions sharing this tree, re-trued continuously, never archived in place. Read it for the lattice (G0..G5) and the red-first procedure; this carrier neither repeats nor edits it.
* ''The hearth ledger'' — <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths">>. It answers ''who holds what · what each owes · what crossed'', and a hearth names a session by its `Claude-Session:` commit trailer. ''The operator authorised this crew's own row; it landed in `0ba716cab`, with C4 scope updated in `0d5deb15c`.'' That permission does not authorise rewriting another hearth's row. The crew still reads #/the-only-guard before touching shared ground.

''Seating the house.'' `lares vessel stand --codex` wires the OpenAI Codex home: the LARES MCP seat, the session-ingest hook, and the BOOT POINTER into `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` (`packages/lares-cli/src/codex-wire.ts:1-24`, `:51`). The pointer aims at the boot carrier rather than copying it — `codex-wire.ts:15-20` states the reason: ''a copied seed is a second seed, and a second seed drifts from the carrier with nothing watching it''. The wire also REAPS a stale `[mcp_servers.mempalace]` block (`:61-68`), because a harness holding its own palace holder reaches past the node into the store and N writers on one Chroma index is what corrupts it. The carrier the pointer names: <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot">>.

''The reading order for a cold hand.''

# #/the-only-guard — commit isolation, before any commit.
# #/traps — the instrument-lies this tree measured and paid for.
# #/standing-on-the-operators-hand — so nothing gets built against an unruled fork.
# #/the-cut — what the founding hearth keeps, so no work collides.
# #/next-steps — current priority and test terrain; #/completed — finished increments and their limits.
# The four sets, #/set-a-mechanical onward, retain the deeper open-item scouts; re-read their older measurements before implementing.

