!! ▶ Act — the next bounded measurement

''Gaia-side story — the steward at the material shore.'' A keeper tending one named lararium can inspect the addressable boot artifact when the browser vessel stays dark: which post-corpus phase completed, whether a worker stood, whether the manifest crossed, and which answer never returned. The trace lets the keeper repair the named boundary rather than treating a local failure as a property of the whole DreamNet. The same grain governs B10: a keeper importing a partly unreadable carrier sees the fenced artifact and preserves the family member the write actually touched.

''Elyncia-side story — the traveler at a living, local shrine.'' A traveler reaches a fed, flickering, or isolated lararium after a road breaks. The node may answer locally while the wider lattice stays absent; it names that condition, receives an offering proportionately, and never manufactures a far-side answer. A damaged ahu arrives as a visible, inert quoteblock at the write's own grain, so the shrine preserves the family and the traveler can bring the wound to a keeper. The sidebar rune returning its sign and the founding rite waiting on its first breath remain separate events; follow the missing response without inventing one.

''Definition of done.'' Extend the nearest existing surface, assert setup, read the intended red, retain positive and deliberate-weakening controls, then implement the smallest cure. Preserve independent failure statuses. Do not widen into the operator-held forks or deferred MCP work.

''Operator's flow law, 2026-09-17.'' Every active hand carries the causal-island law: no global now, and no `Date.now()` or wall clock in load-bearing code; clocks may testify locally, never establish shared order or authority. The stack stays Web3 local-first and capability/crypto-identity/wealth oriented, with cryptofinance illth excluded. A CRDT or non-CRDT conflict reconvenes talk story for the humans; no agent silently picks its outcome. TW5 remains the engine inside isolated worker VMs. `@lararium/mesh` carries intent-level, all-vessel contracts while `@lararium/tw5` carries VM implementation; platform shores stay at node or browser. Workers and projections remain nameless entities composed from `#has` capability stacks. Write chat and code comments under L-Prime. After each major commit, run and record a full ↺ aftermath/cleanup loop as a separate commit when it changes an artifact, then continue flow. When confidence drops sharply, send a lower-family research spirit for outside negentropy before widening a cure.

!! ↺ Hoʻoko / aftermath

''AFTERMATH / YIN, 2026-09-15.'' The runner sweep adds owned-process-group cleanup, app readiness controls and a fake-tool regression wired into the hosted browser job. Herm setup, readiness probes, evidence capture and teardown gain deadlines. Both fake-tool regression files passed; shell syntax, workflow YAML parsing and carrier canonical checks passed. Readiness now requires the owned Vite startup announcement before a bounded HTTP probe, including a delayed foreign-port control. These local runner controls do not supply a hosted workflow receipt. The ledger now carries the enacted crossings carveout and the completed W3 state; the A2 scout separates ordinary founding from the climbed-founder case.

''Approved flowstates, 2026-09-16.'' C4 now carries a test-local manifest-timing witness: `ready → manifest` passes for an immediate browser worker, the 1,500 ms Node compatibility fallback remains explicit, and a delayed browser `ready` records `manifest → ready` as an unresolved race candidate. A2 puts each vessel under its own `LAR_ROOT`, consumes `runInit`'s returned bootstrap path and rejects the stale genesis location; node typechecking passes, while the real opt-in mesh run still owes its isolated window. C1's `where` now probes typed slots even when canon is mounted; its mounted-canon/working-slot witness and TW5 typecheck pass. W5 stays unclaimed.

''Projection follow-up, source audit rather than a reproduced product red.'' `tw5-projection.ts` adds render IDs to a module-level map without retiring detached nodes. The unknown-ID control proves only unknown-ID handling. Next, render a valid target, detach it, send its former ID, and test that no handler fires; retain a live-target positive control. Also tighten the witness's frame ordering and worker-error attribution: a same-worker frame alone does not establish causation, and an unrelated worker fault must not convict the unknown-ID probe. Preserve named state transitions and the disabled-message control. Ensure CI supplies the generated TW5 core so the retained-reveal fixture executes rather than skips.

W3 closes under its named actions and measured limits. D3 gains source wiring, with hosted execution still owed. C4 boot stalls, W5's node-disk leg, full Python-suite health and admitted relay proof remain separate debts. The deeper scouts below retain their historical measurements rather than claiming a fresh full audit.

