<<~ ahu #/the-only-guard>>

! Commit isolation — the ONLY guard between hands

''A hearth names a SESSION, and a session runs many hands.'' The hearth gate reads commit trailers, so it ''cannot see a hand''. Within one hearth it refuses nothing, and it refuses nothing CORRECTLY — hands under one hearth share one intent. What follows binds absolutely: ''within a hearth, commit isolation stands as the whole guard'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths#/law">>).

* `git commit --only -- <explicit file list>`. Never `git add -A`, never a directory pathspec, never `git stash` on this tree. A hand reaching for `git add -A` inside a busy hearth meets no refusal and takes a sibling's half-written file with it.
* An untracked file wants `git add -N <path>` first, then `--only`.
* ''A sibling's commit reads like a stranger's.'' A hand watching the log mid-flight meets commits it never wrote, on files it never touched, under its own trailer. ''Read the trailer, not the surprise'' — a differing trailer names another hearth; an identical one names a sibling hand.
* Commit subjects start `lar:///word.word.word — summary`. Write the message to a FILE and pass `git commit -F <file>`: a backtick in a `-m` string fails SILENTLY.
* ''`dist/` and `bags/` carry other writers, usually the operator.'' Read `git status` before believing any red, and before believing any green that follows one. A dirty file of unknown provenance gets REPORTED and copied aside — never reverted, never committed.

''Two submodules stand operator-deferred as of this writing'' — `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` and `mempalace` both read dirty in the parent, and the operator adjudicates that dirt separately. Touch neither, nor `.worktrees/`.

