<<~ ahu #/set-a-mechanical>>

! Set A — mechanical, enumerable, a worked example stands

!! A1 · The board reads keyed on a vessel key — 12 sites, 7 files

''What it is.'' A per-Nexus deterministic board addressed by the vessel's OWN verifying key (`await loadVesselVerifyingKey(dir)`) instead of by the resolved Nexus island. A Nexus holds no key of its own, so the charter's genesis epoch — a KERI AID every holder derives alike — names the island; `nodeNexusIsland` composes that resolution (`packages/lararium-node/src/nexus-standing.ts:80`).

''RULED, twice, and the two rulings answer different questions.''

* `c6cfe5b8d` (`lar:///one-crossroads.serves.one-nexus`, 2026-09-03) settles ''the PARAMETER''. It touches only `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/unbuilt-laws.test.ts` (+35) and rules N boards the design, never a defect: ''One crossroads serves ONE Nexus… no confederation-wide floor exists, by design''. Its load-bearing close: ''`device-admit` is not that leg: it carries a `hearthDaemonUrl` and no nexus key, because it admits a DEVICE to a fleet rather than a VESSEL to a Nexus.''
* `91ce09afb` (`lar:///the-island.names.no-vessel`, 2026-09-13) settles ''the BOARD''. Every per-Nexus board keys on the NEXUS; three states stand, with ''no nexus → own key as a PRIVATE NEXUS OF ONE'' as a ''stated fact, never a fallback''.

''The worked example.'' `5251f49b2` (`lar:///the-door.stands.where-it-boots`) enacts both at one door: `personaKelBoardDocUrl(await loadVesselVerifyingKey(dir))` becomes `personaKelBoardDocUrl(admitBoardIsland(founderVesselKey))` (`device-admit.ts:69-70`, consumed `:166-167`), the boot COMPOSES the same resolver so no third copy drifts (`open-node-vessel.ts:629-636`), and the parameter stays absent so `c6cfe5b8d` holds. Read the reasoning restated in source at `device-admit.ts:37-68`.

''Read the weld before touching a site'' — `packages/lararium-node/tests/device-admit-reads-the-resolved-island.test.ts:150-171`. It asserts the composed resolver EXISTS AND EXPORTS on the module that owns it (''a token-only weld cannot tell a rename from a deletion''), asserts the door composes it, then sweeps every `personaKelBoardDocUrl(` ARGUMENT for a raw vessel key. ''It strips comments first, and that is a measured trap, never tidiness'': the docblock above `admitBoardIsland` NAMES the old spelling in order to explain why it was wrong, and the sweep matched that prose and red over code already correct. And it pins its own strip against vacuity — `expect(code, "the comment strip ate the file — the sweep below would pass vacuously").toMatch(/personaKelBoardDocUrl\(/)`.

''The sites that stand, every one spelled `const nexusPubkey = await loadVesselVerifyingKey(<dir>)``, and every one under `packages/lararium-node/src/` — none under `packages/lares-cli/src/`.''

