''The answer to the walk's question: the console LOGS the carry; the gate does not throw.'' On a vessel founded offline and later handed a gate key, `nexusIdentity` resolves scope to the anchor and `nexusIslandsBelow` (`nexus-identity.ts:261-283`, the third narrowing at `:270` nulling `anchorGateKey`) returns the vessel's own key as the island below. So `open-browser-vessel.ts:885-888` runs the carry immediately before the gate read (''which is the whole cure'', `:874`), and `persona-kel-climb.ts:104` prints `[persona-kel] carried N event(s) for <prefix>… up the gradient …`, returning `{ carried, from: island }` at `:107`. Idempotent: `:84` returns `nothing` at the bottom of the gradient, `:91` returns `nothing` when the destination already carries the chain (every later boot), `:99` `console.warn`s an island that would not open. ''The throw survives as the FALLBACK'' — `open-browser-vessel.ts:891-892` reds fail-closed with ''persona-KEL chain … absent from the local board — the Binding Gate cannot reach a head'', reachable now only when the carry finds nothing below, which is the pre-cure brick.

''Earlier scout state (now superseded by the witness below).'' All fifteen vectors in `nexus-board-climb-at-leaf.test.ts` drive synthetic repos and boards (`:121-414`) or read the boot's SOURCE TEXT: the fault-pin at `:452` reads the boot with `?raw` (`:58`) and asserts ordering by `indexOf` at `:507-511`, with the −1 hazard called out at `:505`. At that reading no test or e2e walked found-offline → configure-the-anchor → reload in a real browser, so the source pin alone held the wiring. The held-out `browser-weld` surface was the stated precondition; it now carries the C4 walk described next.

''The held-out walk now stands as a real-browser harness, and the full five-vector run passed.'' `tools/browser-weld/leaf-continuity.mjs`, invoked after the ordinary weld by `tools/browser-weld-witness.sh`, opens a fresh persistent Chromium profile against the NORMAL Vite app. Its ordinary vector reads the private Binding-Gate chain through a test-only fetched-module observation (no production debug door), then proves: offline founding → `?gate=` anchor → document reload preserves the same `0x` device DID and the same non-empty ordered event-CID sequence; the first anchor boot logs the one KEL carry and the reload logs none. Its fault vector replaces the ONE exact `carryPersonaKelUpTheGradient` call in its fetched module and demands the existing fail-closed missing-chain halt. Its malformed-anchor vector reaches the exact `nexusScopeOrThrow` TORN/no-board door, then retries a valid anchor and demands the original DID+CIDs. The isolated normal-app Chromium run passed C4.1 offline identity, C4.2 anchored carry, C4.3 idempotent reload, C4.4 disabled-carry refusal, and C4.5 malformed scope-door + valid retry: `pnpm --filter @lararium/app exec vite --host 127.0.0.1 --port 5182` (one terminal), then `WELD_APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5182 LEAF_BOOT_MS=30000 node tools/browser-weld/leaf-continuity.mjs` (another). Earlier attempts at an isolated Vite port stalled after `corpus-ready` with the DOM still `booting…`; the final run did not reproduce that intermittent observation, and this handoff does not infer its cause. This proof covers local browser continuity; relay admission needs another boundary: `?gate=` scopes the local leaf's Nexus, while a real crossing still requires an explicit `?relay=` service.

!! D1 · Python-suite CI wiring; full-run receipt still owed

''TAKEN 2026-09-15 — `24366c5f6` (`lar:///the-sensorium.reaches-the-python-suite`).'' The `test` job now installs `pytest` into the holder venv and runs `~/.venv/bin/python3 -m pytest packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts -q`. Its regression vector lives at `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/test_ci_sensorium_suite.py`: it REDDED first because the workflow named no sensorium-holder step, then GREENED only after that exact venv invocation landed. Re-derived collection: 990 cases before this vector's one added case; do not preserve the old 962-function number as a CI total.

''The handoff's 962-test observation.'' Derived: `def test_` across 96 files under `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts` — ''note the path, `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts`, never a top-level `lararium-sensorium/`''. All 962 of the package's python tests live under `scripts/`; the only python outside it carries none (`mempalace_source_lares/{__init__,adapter}.py`). Collected count runs slightly HIGHER than 962 — eight `@pytest.mark.parametrize` decorators expand some functions (`test_loci_io.py:251,258` · `test_stream_events.py:137` · `test_capture_session.py:281` · `test_structure_router.py:35,72` · `qa_anchor/tests/test_dprime.py:51` · `qa_anchor/tests/test_reliability.py:95`).

''The workflow reading at handoff.'' At the original scout, two workflows stood — `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and `notify-pages.yml`. `pytest` appeared in `ci.yml` only as `pip install tree-sitter pytest pygls` — an INSTALL — and the only step that then ran it was the grammar host's `pnpm run gate:fold`, a different package. The `test` job ran `pnpm test` → root `package.json:9` `pnpm -r … test`, and `packages/lararium-sensorium/package.json` declares `"test": "vitest run"` — ''vitest only''. Sensorium carries 2 `.test.ts` files. Its holder venv then only installed `mempalace` and asserted its import.

''Trap:'' `pnpm -r test` SKIPS the root `tests/` directory BY DESIGN — the workspace runs wider than `packages/*`.

''D1 verification limit.'' The focused CI regression passed. This crew did not complete a full holder-suite run; wiring the command does not certify suite health.

