<<~ ahu #/traps>>

! The traps this tree already paid for

''Each one below stands MEASURED — an instrument that read green while reporting something false, or a habit that cost hours. Collide each before trusting it.''

!! Test-design traps

''A control set made only of negatives reads satisfied by INERTNESS.'' Measured: `priorIslands: []` killed a carry outright while all eight behavioural vectors stayed GREEN. `packages/lararium-node/tests/nexus-board-climb-at-boot.test.ts:30`, `:370` name it, and the cure at `:363-394` is a FAULT-PIN over the call's own arguments, not another behavioural vector. The same weakening rides the leaf boot (C4).

''A red proving the hole exists does not prove the fix holds.'' Add a pin that bites a WEAKENING, not the original hole. The worked pin (`nexus-board-climb-at-boot.test.ts:363-394`) holds five clauses: ① a CENSUS, `calls.length === 1` · ② the call must name `nexusIslandsBelow(nexusStandsAt)`, never a literal · ③ three forbidden boards asserted ABSENT from the call · ④ the NESTING measured by indentation depth, so the climb cannot slip under a guard · ⑤ the ordering.

''An ordering assertion over an absent call passes VACUOUSLY.'' `indexOf` answers −1, and −1 sits below everything. Both worked pins carry the hazard in a comment (`nexus-board-climb-at-boot.test.ts:391-394` · `nexus-board-climb-at-leaf.test.ts:505`). An ordering clause wants a presence clause beside it.

''Run the nonsense control.'' Feed the gate something that MUST fail — a nonsense verb, a mangled digest, an address nothing holds. A control that passes proves the gate reads nothing, and a green from a gate that reads nothing carries no information.

''Assert the setup took.'' A fixture mutating a live carrier MUST assert its own mutation landed (`.not.toBe(source)`). A silent no-op replace leaves disk == synced == canonical, and four vectors then agree with each other about nothing.

''A fixture that DECLARES is a carrier.'' The finder reads the DOCTYPE / `type` line, never the path. Three witnesses ate themselves in a week. Assemble the declaration at read time, and CONTROL that the finder reads false.

!! Source-reading welds

''A source-reading weld is not behaviour.'' Measured both directions in `dbb6d7ec1`: one weld SURVIVED a deliberate rename because it takes a CENSUS (`calls.length === 2`) of every call site, so renaming a loader drops the count and ungating one stops the prefix matching. The other ''went GREEN over a loop that only warns to stdout'' — its `src.slice(at, at + 900)` window reached ~120 characters PAST the loop's closing braces, and a dead `if (false)` branch carrying a matching call sat in the slack. ''Window by BRACE MATCHING from the anchor'', which has no slack to hide a decoy in and no length to outgrow.

''Strip comments FIRST, and pin the strip.'' `packages/lararium-node/tests/device-admit-reads-the-resolved-island.test.ts:161-167`: a docblock NAMING an old spelling in order to explain why it was wrong made a sweep red over code already correct — ''a weld reading raw source cannot tell an explanation of a defect from the defect''. And assert the strip left something (`:167-168`), or the sweep below passes vacuously.

''Prefer a CENSUS.'' `calls.length === N` cannot be greened by a rename. A token match can.

''A grep for callers counts MENTIONS'', including comments that say the caller does not exist. Follow the call; never grep the door.

!! Reading and reasoning traps

''A law whose REASON measurement refutes ERODES'' — because the next reader corrects the reason and keeps the conclusion. Worked: `59212d29e` found the archive-write omission resting on ''a browser vessel holds no fs'', which measurement reads FALSE (OPFS is a filesystem and that very shore already writes it). The conclusion survived on a DIFFERENT ground — CUSTODY — and now retires ''on a condition rather than on a platform claim''. State the invariant; when a reason falls, re-ground it or drop the law.

''A conjunction is an argument, never a measurement.'' `b14fbbc4d`: six conjunctive gates priced their own trade with zero samples. The measurement (ZERO false positives over 200 real archives, 2,192,000 bytes) came with PROVENANCE named rather than implied, and the shipped test re-derives it at a named `SAMPLES` ''so the figure can be re-derived rather than re-trusted''.

''THE PIN-READER LAW: null means "no default owed", never "something is wrong".'' Two live guards fell to `?? []` / `?? emptyDoc()` over a reader whose null means ABSENT ''or'' TORN. Ask of every default: does it STATE a fact or LOSE one? `bulb-read-face.ts:220-221`'s `heads: []` STATES a fact (no CRDT log) — copying a stamp onto it would lose that.

''MEASURE BOTH SIDES OF A BOUNDARY.'' A wire that DROPS a field may not LOSE it — the receiver re-derives. With a first-writer-wins store, read-ORDER runs load-bearing: the read may fail while the record stands.

''A commit subject is a CLAIM, never evidence.'' And a reader stricter than the parser still reads as a lying reader.

''DERIVE, never enumerate.'' Every count in #/set-d-infrastructure carries its derivation for exactly this reason, and three of the four numbers this hearth was handed measured wrong.

!! Tree and run traps

''Never run two e2e sets at once'' — they share a mutable `synced-tree.json` (`packages/lararium-node/src/island-behaviors.ts:43`, `join(larProjectionDir(), "synced-tree.json")`; the law stated at `open-node-vessel.ts:2277`). Per-suite green hid a clobbered shared tree for two days, reading 6 red files on the whole set. ''Check `pgrep -af witness` and `pgrep -af vitest` before any run.'' RUN THE WHOLE SET; BISECT in a worktree, never guess; an import failure reads as 0 tests, never as a pass.

''`lares vessel stand` DETACHES.'' It spawns detached-and-unref'd so a hook never blocks on a long-lived daemon, and readiness reads SELF-ATTESTED from the node's own log — `phase → vessel-ready` on success, `fatal:` on a boot fault. ''Read `<lares>/vessel/stand.log` from the byte offset the run starts appending at, never the launcher's pipe'' (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/stand.ts:234-250`; the read worked at `tests/e2e/herm-floor.test.ts:91-97` and `tests/e2e/vessel-sealed.test.ts:159`).

''`witness-all`'s last line lies; capture `$?`.'' The script deliberately never short-circuits (`tools/witness-all.sh:1-6`) and exits the WORST status — but the ''held out of this run'' block prints AFTER the per-witness runs, so on a failure the benign roster is the last thing on screen and ''witness-all: every witness clean'' simply never appears. ''And a pipe's `$?` is the last stage's'' — `ci.yml:206-209` pipes through `tee`, which is why the roll-call gate greps the log rather than trusting an exit code.

''`dist/` and `bags/` stand SHARED MUTABLE.'' Typecheck reads SOURCE and the binary reads DIST, so a cross-package wire passes typecheck and dies at runtime whenever `dist/` lags — run the BUILT binary after any cross-package rename. ''A revert-verify that swaps source only reads VACUOUS against an e2e.'' And know what your import resolves to: `@lararium/mesh` reads SRC under the node package's vitest aliases and DIST under lares-cli's, so the same symbol ''missing'' names a stale dist rather than absent code.

''NEVER touch `~/.local/share/lares`. Isolate with `LAR_ROOT`.'' ''CORRECTION, measured — `LAR_ROOT` alone DOES isolate every XDG kind.'' Each resolver tests it FIRST: `larStateHome` (`packages/lararium-node/src/vessel-paths.ts:82-86`) · `larCacheHome` (`:89-93`) · `larConfigHome` (`:96-100`) · `larRuntimeHome` (`:103-107`) · `larHome` (`:130-131`) · `laresDataHome` and `larariumDataHome` (`packages/lararium-mempalace/src/xdg-base.ts:29-32`, `:57-60`). Setting `XDG_STATE_HOME`/`XDG_DATA_HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME` beside it reads as belt-and-braces, never as the thing that makes isolation work.

''What `LAR_ROOT` does NOT isolate — this is the real hazard, and one of these reaches a DESTRUCTIVE verb.''

* `~/.mempalace`, the GUEST store parent, LAR_ROOT-blind at `packages/lararium-mempalace/src/xdg-base.ts:73`, `packages/lares-cli/src/commands/mempalace.ts:47`, and ''`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/mempalace-repave.ts:40`''.
* `~/.venv` (`packages/lararium-mempalace/src/spawn-resolve.ts:44`; `packages/lares-cli/src/link-bin.ts:38`) and `~/.local/bin` (`vessel-paths.ts:122`; `link-bin.ts:43,65,102,105`).
* The harness homes `~/.claude`, `~/.codex`, `~/.copilot`. The wires accept an injectable `opts.home` (`claude-wire.ts:181,301,339` · `codex-wire.ts:51` · `copilot-wire.ts:50` · `vscode-wire.ts:87`) and DEFAULT to `homedir()`; the harvest reader takes no injection at all (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/harvest.ts:524`, `:624`). ''A `lares vessel stand --codex` under `LAR_ROOT` still writes the operator's real `~/.codex`.''

''Never read the passphrase file.''

!! Character and rename traps

''WELD TEST before any rename'' — grep the signing domains FIRST. A rename that moves a signing domain changes bytes every peer verifies.

''TAMPER PROBES move DECODED bytes.'' Assert the ENCODING changed first, or the probe measures nothing.

''CHARACTER SWEEPS hit four classes.'' Fence the RELATION, and re-stamp the block checks afterward.

''A blanket re-stamp signs edits nobody authored.'' `lares meme normalize` names its files and takes no glob, because a re-stamp driven by `git diff` signs the OTHER writer's work — and it NAMES every dirty carrier a run passed over, since a carrier nobody named reads two ways and the door cannot tell which.

