! Where the framing this hearth handed over measured WRONG

''Carried openly, because a crew building on a false pointer pays for it twice.'' Each correction below stands measured on 2026-09-14; the item that carries it names the evidence.

|!the framing handed over |!what measurement reads |
|nine CLI verbs on the wrong-key board |''12 sites across 7 files'', all under `packages/lararium-node/src/`, none under `packages/lares-cli/src/`. ''Nine'' counts the sites `91ce09afb` CURED (nine in `open-node-vessel`, six in `open-browser-vessel`, two in `init.ts`), never the sites left standing. And two of the 12 (`boot-invite-burn.ts:74`, `:95`) read NO board — A1 |
|`tests/e2e/two-vessel-mesh` reds on an unbuilt `social-bootstrap.json` |It lives at `packages/lararium-node/tests/e2e/`, and the red reads a STALE PATH: `runInit` writes to `larBootstrapPath()` and ignores its `genesisDir` argument, so the test reads a path nothing writes — A2 |
|`herm-reshares-public-blob` — 1 `beforeAll` death, climb cures unverified |The `beforeAll` does not throw; it stashes a `standGate` and the first test names the verdict. ''And the announce-plane fork stands RULED AND CURED'' (`open-node-vessel.ts:2272-2277`) — the shift ledger's ''one MORE ruling owed'' reads stale. What stands owed reads narrower and is named in source: ⑦ UNMEASURED against the cure, and the Herm holding no carriage CLIENT — A3 |
|break (c) — which key signs a floor that seats no persona? |MISFRAMED. Break (c) names the UNSIGNED-announcement attack pair, and its own cure reads ''the floor's announcement MUST sign''. The which-key half stands answered by `SEATED ⊥ RAISED` plus the Place-DID heraldry ruling. What waking-floor leaves open: what ''recognition'' means, and the renewal interval — ⑥ |
|the `anchors-h{N}` census |MISFRAMED. No carrier names such a census (zero grep hits). Anchors sit out of the key census BY LAW (public doc-ids, no seal), enumeration rides an explicit roster never a dir-scan, and the opposite discipline stands ruled for the secret h{N} family — ⑦ |
|the crossings-deadlock's permanent shape |''ALREADY RULED.'' Cure ① landed at `0d00d75f5`, enacted in `tools/hearths-gate.mjs:93-95` and welded at `tools/hearths-gate-witness.sh:146`. the aftermath sweep reconciled the ledger prose — ⑤ |
|`02d7f24bf` rules `bag-residency.ts`'s home |It rules the ADJACENT word collision and says of this item, verbatim, ''with the fork between them left OPEN'' — ④ |
|DEPARTURE's record must NAME the island it left |The source requires the ABSENCE be named by an act at the rite. Naming the departed island reads as a DESIGN PROPOSAL, never quoted law — B3 |
|the hostful forms COLLIDE on disk |They cannot collide today: hostful fails `startsWith("lar:///")` and never sites. The pair reads IRRECONCILABLE — hostful un-projectable forward, every disk file deriving back as hostless. The collision reads LATENT, arriving the day something sites a hostful URI by stripping only the scheme — B8 |
|a reserved segment + Go-style `!`-escaping for case |''No carrier holds either idea'' — zero hits repo-wide for every spelling. Oral prior art; write it down before building against it. And `lar-uri-namespace.mem:45` (''The authority prefix resolves the collision'') reads FALSE against `bag-paths.ts:97` — B8 |
|a flattened `.mem` carries `uri-path`, never `title:` |A flattened `.mem` carries NEITHER, and that absence is precisely why it flattens. The pairing describes the RULED/LOCI carrier, which is the one not uniquified — B9 |
|`wiki-layer-ontology#/alpha-transition` carries five stages |It carries no staged plan and no numbered stages. Its one ordering statement reads ''the hand-edit weld lands LAST and stays silent throughout''; derive the stages from the ruling and the artifacts — C1 |
|`lares wiki which <title>`: working ⟺ working present; fallback ⟺ bags alone |It takes a tiddler URI and decides nothing; the daemon's `where` reactor decides. The forward direction holds; the reverse does NOT — `worker-data-verbs.ts:100` short-circuits before the slot probe for any wiki whose canon bag already mounts in the composite — C1 |
|`vessel-regions.mem` — no test pins the boot order |True of the four reds, and too strong as written: `nexus-board-climb-at-boot.test.ts:391-394` pins a source-text ordering over a different ordering. And the meme's own line cites read stale — `prepareNodeBoot` at `:371`, the file at 2311 lines — B6 |
|the browser corpus: 0 new files over 391 carriers |Holds, and the 391/0 reading lives in `bfcf8bd58`'s commit message and nowhere else — un-re-measurable from the tree. And 391 / 701 / 708 / 655+46 count FOUR different populations — C3 |
|989 python tests |''962'' `def test_` across 96 files, collected slightly higher through 8 parametrize decorators. The no-workflow-reach half holds — D1 |
|the witness fleet runs 29 of 33 |''30 of 35.'' `ci.yml`'s own comment reads 34, itself stale — D2 |
|five held-out witnesses |''Five stands right'' where the earlier shift ledger's four was stale (`mesh-scenarios` joined). Previously unscheduled; `held-out.yml` now wires weekly/manual runs, with hosted execution still owed — D3 |
|`larHome()` honours `LAR_ROOT` alone, so set the XDG vars too |''Inverted.'' Every XDG resolver in the stack tests `LAR_ROOT` FIRST, so `LAR_ROOT` alone isolates state, cache, config, run, and both data houses. The real hazard reads `~/.mempalace` (including the destructive `mempalace repave`), `~/.venv`, `~/.local/bin`, and the harness homes — #/traps |
|`foldOfferingAntigen` at `offering-antigen.ts:129-150` |The body ends at `:146`; the meme repeats `:150` in four places — B1 |

