! What a fresh hand reads first

# #/the-only-guard, then #/traps. Both before the first commit and before the first vector.
# <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot">> — the house entire.
# <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/handoff">> `#/shift-founding-watch` — the RED-FIRST test design as eight ordered moves, and the ladder for wiring a module that stands designed, tested and unreached. Both still govern every vector and every wire in this carrier.
# <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/hearths">> — who holds what, including this crew's authorised row.
# #/next-steps, then #/completed — current priorities before the deeper scouts, finished receipts before re-opening an item.
# #/standing-on-the-operators-hand — before designing against any fork.
# <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/registry-filter">> — the law that rejects a fork at design time. A compiled-about registry at ANY scope refuses.

''Naming law, carried from the shift ledger.'' Until a production path calls it, a module stands ''specified in code'' — never ''built'', never ''done'', never ''ready''. Three of the items in this carrier (B1's fold, B7's adapters, D4's decoder) sit exactly there.

''Pointer checks carry a bounded claim.'' `tools/source-pointer.mjs` checks explicit `source-file` metadata and source edges across tracked carriers. It does not validate this handoff's inline file/line citations or prove their claims. Open each named source before acting; rerun the pointer tool after changes to explicit source edges.

